Title: How can I "inject" one model into another?
Description: Alright, this may seem kind of crazy but please try to follow along.  I'm hoping there's a simple solution.

I've found that when providing a complete "document" to my angular client of a user account...

```
User.find(
    {
        where:whereObj,
        order: '"People"."gender" DESC',
        include:[
            {
                model: Person,
                as: "People",
                include:[
                    {
                        model: PersonalTrait,
                        as: "Traits"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                model: Media,
                as: "PrimaryMedia"
            },
            {
                model: MediaFolder,
                as: "MediaFolders",
                include:[
                    {
                        model: Media,
                        as: "Media"
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    }
).success(function(user){
    if(user === null){
        res.send(404);
    }else{
        res.json(200, user);
   }
}).error(function(err){
    res.send(400);
});
```

I see the database query resulting in exponential rows, depending on the number of rows for Traits, MediaFolders and Media.  For example...  1 User row has 2 People rows and 2 MediaFolder rows produces 4 rows in Sequelize's query to produce the object.  Adding 2 MediaRows linked to a MediaFolder row produces 6 rows. Adding 2 Traits to the User now produces 9 rows.  20 traits = 63 rows.  20 traits & 12 media = 252 rows.

I'm fairly certain I understand why this is and that I'm using Sequelize properly.  So I decided to try taking a different approach by first getting the basic User object with everything but the Media Folders, then getting those media folders and "injecting" them into the User object result.

```
User.find(
    {
        where:whereObj,
        order: '"People"."gender" DESC',
        include:[
            {
                model: Person,
                as: "People",
                include:[
                    {
                        model: PersonalTrait,
                        as: "Traits"
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                model: Media,
                as: "PrimaryMedia"
            }
        ]
    }
).success(function(user){
    if(user === null){
        res.send(404);
    }else{

        MediaFolder.findAll(
            {
                where: {
                    "UserId": user.id
                },
                include:[
                    {
                        model: Media,
                        as: "Media"
                    }
                ]
            }
        ).success(function(mediaFolders){
            user.mediaFolders = mediaFolders; // <-- pseudocode
            res.json(200, user);
        }).error(function(err){
            res.send(400);
        });
   }
}).error(function(err){
    res.send(400);
});
```

The only problem is that I'm not sure how I can do this because that "pseudocode" line above didn't work.  :)


